      "safe_claims": [
        "The roof shelters interior spaces and controls moisture, heat, and air flow.",
        "Roof form and slope must match the roofing material used to shed water toward drains, gutters, or downspouts.",
        "Flat roofs require continuous membrane roofing, recommended minimum slope of 1/4 inch per foot or 1:50, and drainage to drains or scuppers.",
        "Low-slope roofs require roll or continuous membrane roofing; medium- and high-slope roofs may use shingles, tiles, or sheet materials.",
        "Roof systems carry gravity loads, rain/snow loads where applicable, equipment loads, and wind uplift, and may need fire resistance and thermal/moisture control."
      ],
      "use_limits": [
